course: dictionary
lesson: 1604
title: Cheerful: happy and bright
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Cheerful is a happy word. A cheerful person is happy and in a good mood, and shows it with smiles and a friendly manner. «A cheerful smile» is a smile that shows someone feels good.
explain: Cheerful can also describe things. «Cheerful yellow curtains» are bright and pleasant, and they make a room feel happy. A cheerful song sounds bright and makes you feel good.
explain: A word can describe how something looks or sounds, not always how it behaves. «That cheerful robin is also one of the fiercest birds in the garden» means the robin looks bright and lively, but it will still fight other robins to keep its patch.
explain: Use the swap test. Put happy into the sentence: «bright yellow curtains» still makes sense, so cheerful means bright and pleasant here. If the meaning does not fit, check the words around it again.
fact: Cheerful means happy and in a good mood.
fact: A cheerful person shows it with smiles and a friendly manner.
fact: A cheerful place, colour or song is bright and pleasant and makes you feel happy.
fact: Cheerful is an adjective: cheerful, more cheerful, most cheerful.
fact: «A cheerful tune» can sound happy even when the words are silly or dark, like «Alouette», which is about plucking a lark's feathers.
exercise: «The cheerful children waved as the bus pulled in.» What does cheerful mean here? | *Happy and in a good mood | Lost and worried | Angry and loud | Tired and sleepy
exercise: «Cheerful yellow curtains brightened the kitchen.» What does cheerful describe? | *The curtains, which are bright and pleasant | The sound of the oven | The wind outside | The cold floor
exercise: «That cheerful robin is also one of the fiercest birds in the garden.» Find and copy the word that means most fierce. | *fiercest | garden | birds | robin
test: «Ella gave a cheerful greeting when she met her friends.» What does this suggest about Ella? | She was asleep | She was lost | She was angry with them | *She was in a good mood and friendly
test: Which of these is a cheerful place? | A silent room with grey walls | *A bright, sunny playground | A dark, damp cellar | A cold, muddy ditch
exam: The robin is called cheerful, but it also fights other robins. What does this teach you? | Cheerful means angry | Cheerful always means nice | *A word can describe how something looks or sounds, not always how it behaves | Robins are never fierce
